title: Customize a Table
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

TiddlyWiki's table syntax is great for short, regular tables. For complex tables with `colgroup`, scope attributes, or multi-line cells, you need full HTML. Custom-markup gives you a more readable middle path. The recipe is to define a set of markers, one per HTML table tag, then write the table with them.

!! Goal

Produce something like:

```
<table>
	<caption>Superheros and sidekicks</caption>
	<tr>
		<th>Power</th>
		<th>Batman</th>
		<th>Flash</th>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<th scope="row">Skill</th>
		<td>Smarts</td>
		<td>Super speed</td>
	</tr>
</table>
```

!! Option 1: marker tiddlers (canonical, vocabulary-engine)

Add five marker tiddlers tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker>>:

|! Marker |! `open` |! `kind` |! `mode` |! `element` |! `end-string` |
|TABLE |`TABLE` |`word` |`block` |`table` |`---` |
|CAPTION |`CAPTION` |`word` |`inline` |`caption` | |
|ROW |`ROW` |`word` |`block` |`tr` |`--` |
|TH |`TH` |`word` |`inline` |`th` | |
|TD |`TD` |`word` |`inline` |`td` | |

Group all five under `vocab/table` and add `vocab/table` tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary>> with `marker-tag: vocab/table`. Activate per tiddler:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Table
```

Then write the table:

```
TABLE
CAPTION Superheros and sidekicks
ROW
TH Power
TH Batman
TH Flash
--
ROW
TH Skill
TD Smarts
TD Super speed
--
---
```

`TABLE` terminates at `---`, each `ROW` at `--`, `CAPTION`/`TH`/`TD` at end-of-line. Each `TH`/`TD` consumes the rest of its line as the cell content, so one cell per line.

A worked example lives at [[Example - TABLE word markers]].

!! Option 2: inline pragma (escape hatch)

The same configuration via `\custom` pragmas, scoped to one tiddler. Activate vocab/legacy-glyphs so the tick is available:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs
```

Pragmas at the top:

```
\custom tick=table _element=table _mode=block _endString="---"
\custom tick=caption _element=caption
\custom tick=row _element=tr _mode=block
\custom tick=th _element=th
\custom tick _element=td

´table ´caption Superheros and sidekicks
´row ´th Power ´th Batman ´th Flash

´row ´th Skill ´ Smarts ´ Super speed
---
```

The bare `\custom tick _element=td` registers the default (empty-symbol) tick form as the `td` cell.

See [[Customize a Table with Multiline Content]] for the variant where each cell holds a block of text, and [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the marker-field schema.
